# Scratch files, never part of the site.
#
# _commitmsg.txt is how a multi-line commit message gets to `git commit -F`:
# passing one with `-m` gets it shredded into pathspecs and the commit silently
# does not happen (see CLAUDE.md). It is written, used and deleted — but a
# `git add -A` that runs before the delete will happily commit it, which is
# exactly what happened on 27 Jul 2026.
#
# It matters more here than in most repos: there is no publish directory, so
# the repo root IS the deployed site and anything left here is served at
# adhjrt.com/<filename>.
_commitmsg.txt
_msg*.txt
*.ps1.bak

# Node, if anything ever installs here. The site itself has no build step.
node_modules/
